# IDP package rules

- **Alias:** Use `@blocks-idp/<domain>/...` where `<domain>` is `authentication`, `iam`, `mfa`, or `captcha`. Mapped in root `tsconfig.json` to `./idp/*`.
- **Not standalone:** IDP imports `@/components`, `@/lib`, `@/store`, and other `@blocks-*` packages. Do not assume `idp/` can build in isolation.
- **UI:** Prefer `@/components/ui-kits/*` (shadcn-style) and existing `@/components/*` helpers. Do not duplicate Button/Form/Dialog primitives inside `idp/`.
- **New route:** Add the screen under `idp/...`, export from a barrel when neighbors do, then add a thin `src/app/.../page.tsx` that imports the IDP component. Use `"use client"` when the component uses hooks or browser APIs.
- **Data:** Add API calls via a `*.service.ts` under the relevant domain and a React Query hook under `hooks/`. Reuse `http` from `@/lib/http-client` and path constants from `idp/**/constants/*endpoint*` or `src/constant/endpoint.constant.ts` (`API_BASES`).
- **Docs:** See `.cursor/docs/idp/README.md` and `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-10-idp-architecture-design.md`. Run `npm run idp:manifest` after large `idp/` tree changes; run `npm run idp:route-map` after new or changed `src/app/**/page.tsx` that import `@blocks-idp`.
